  "id": "COMPOUND:23562 - PROTEIN:585",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that caulerpal A may be involved in the regulation of Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase through multiple pathways. The target entity Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase is engaged by three distinct compounds: 7-Xylosyltaxol, Platambin-1,6-dione, and Boschnialactone, all of which are targets of L-lactate dehydrogenase C chain. This indicates that caulerpal A may act as a modulator or regulator of the L-lactate dehydrogenase C chain, which in turn influences the activity of Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. The scores from the three paths suggest a consistent relationship, with varying levels of confidence, but all pointing toward a potential functional link between caulerpal A and Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. The mechanisms appear to involve the L-lactate dehydrogenase C chain as a central mediator, though the exact nature of the interaction between caulerpal A and this chain remains to be fully elucidated.",
